<title>USA: Allstate to buy back stock.</title>
<headline>Allstate to buy back stock.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHBROOK, Illinois 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Allstate Corp said Thursday its board of directors had approved a new stock repurchase program.</p>
<p>Allstate, parent of Allstate Insurance Co, said in a statement it will buy back up to $2 billion worth of common shares through December 31, 1998.</p>
<p>The new program follows the recently completed $750 million stock repurchase program authorized last year, it said.</p>
<p>Allstate's stock closed 12/16 down at 72-13/16 on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>It has a total of more than 435 million shares.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
